      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:5:5:5",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) بَعِيرٌ تَرَدَّى فِي بِئْرٍ كَيْفَ يُنْحَرُ قَالَ تُدْخِلُ الْحَرْبَةَ فَتَطْعُنُهُ بِهَا وَ تُسَمِّي وَ تَأْكُلُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Humeyd Bin Ziyad, from Al Hassan Bin Muhammad Bin Sama’at, from Ahmad Bin Al Hassan Al Maysamy, from Aban, from Ismail Al Ju’fy who said, ",
          "‘I said to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, ‘A camel fell down in a well, how can it be sacrificed?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Stab it with a bayonet and Name (<span class=\"iTxt\">Bismillah</span>) and eat’."
        ]
      }
    },
